        "title": "Send client version header and add shared experiment bucketing",
        "summary": "The CLI now attaches its version number to Freebuff session requests via the new `FREEBUFF_CLIENT_VERSION_HEADER`, allowing server-side friction logs to correlate refusals with the specific client build that encountered them. This observe-only header is read from `CODEBUFF_CLI_VERSION` and does not alter session behavior. The commit also introduces `common/src/util/stable-bucket.ts` for deterministic user bucketing in Postgres-backed experiments, using FNV-1a hashing with a lowbias32 finalizer to ensure uniform distribution across users with shared ID prefixes. Additionally, `common/src/util/stats.ts` provides dependency-free statistical helpers including Wilson intervals, Newcombe's difference test, and chi-square sample-ratio-mismatch checks for experiment readouts. Two other changes are included in this snapshot: the addition of shared constants and the introduction of new utility modules with their respective test suites.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "maintainers",
        "evidence": "In `cli/src/utils/freebuff-session-api.ts`, the function `requestFreebuffSession` now reads `CODEBUFF_CLI_VERSION` and conditionally sets the `FREEBUFF_CLIENT_VERSION_HEADER` (defined in `common/src/constants/freebuff-desktop-sessions.ts` as 'x-freebuff-client-version') on outgoing session calls. The diff also adds `common/src/util/stable-bucket.ts` containing `experimentBucket`, `armForBucket`, and `validateArmWeights`, and `common/src/util/stats.ts` containing `wilsonInterval`, `newcombeDifference`, and `sampleRatioMismatch`.",
        "userVisible": false,
